.TH M4KK1 7 "Desktop Interaction Guide"
.SH NAME
Desktop interaction guide \- shortcuts, menus and operations of the
Sprach window manager desktop
.SH OVERVIEW
This page describes the M4KK1 desktop environment (Copland display
server + Sprach WM + MDM greeter): the Bar menu, Dock quick launch,
Launchpad, file manager (fm), virtual desktops, wallpaper themes,
system tray and desktop icons.
The \fBRule\fR key is the keyboard Win/Meta key; the current keymap maps
it onto the \fBAlt\fR modifier slot.
.SH BAR MENU
Click the "M4KK1" brand text at the top-left of the Bar to open the
dropdown menu:
.TP
.B About This PC
Info panel with OS/kernel version (uname), total/used/free memory
(sysinfo, KB), build date and CPU model.
.TP
.B System Settings
Opens the wallpaper theme picker: six theme swatches (Classic Blue,
Ocean, Dusk Purple, Graphite, Desert, Forest) in a 2x3 grid with the
active theme highlighted. Clicking a swatch switches the wallpaper
instantly (theme id is shared via copland_shm; both Copland composite
paths repaint) and the desktop icon layer follows.
.TP
.B Lock Screen
Ends the session; the screen returns to the MDM greeter.
.TP
.B Shut Down
After the session ends Copland issues the magic-gated reboot syscall
(int 0x80 nr 0x6D, magic1=0x01234567 magic2=0x89ABCDEF). QEMU std
i386 has no ACPI poweroff; the warm reset is the only machine-level
restart this hardware offers.
.SH DOCK QUICK LAUNCH
.TP
.B Rule+1 .. Rule+9
Activates the Nth Dock icon from the left: raises the existing window
or spawns a new instance.
.SH LAUNCHPAD
Click the Dock grid icon to open the full-screen 4-column app grid.
The app list is scanned at open time from \fI/bin\fR and \fI/usr/bin\fR
(same target, deduplicated), skipping dot-files and WM-internal
components (sprach/copland/login/mdm ...). Each app shows a 32x32
icon (icons.c) and its name. Clicking an icon launches the app and
closes the Launchpad; Esc or a background click closes it too.
.SH FILE MANAGER (fm)
The initial tab opens the user's home directory (the home field of
the passwd.db entry matching the current uid; root -> /export/root).
.TP
.B Ctrl+T / Ctrl+W
New tab / close current tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab
Cycle through the in-use tabs (or click the tab strip directly).
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Focus the address bar, type a path and press Enter; Esc cancels.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Toggle hidden (dot-prefixed) file display.
.TP
.B Enter / j / k
Open the selection / move down / move up.
.TP
.B mouse click / double click
Click selects a row or switches tabs; double click enters a directory
or opens a file.
.TP
File types
Directories use the folder icon, .txt the text icon, .c/.h the code
icon, everything else the generic file icon. Double-clicking a text
file opens the built-in read-only preview (first 24 lines); Esc,
Enter or q leaves it. (m4k_spawn has no argv, so launching sead with
the path is impossible; the preview is the equivalent.)
.SH VIRTUAL DESKTOPS
.TP
.B Rule+Shift+1 / 2 / 3 / 4
Switch to desktop 1\-4. Windows show/hide per their desktop; the Bar
center shows "Desktop N".
.SH WALLPAPER
The MDM greeter and the Sprach desktop background share
\fBgui_draw_wallpaper()\fR: a theme-driven vertical gradient, with the
active theme id shared via copland_shm. Six themes: Classic Blue
(0x000044 -> 0x0066FF), Ocean, Dusk Purple, Graphite, Desert, Forest.
Switch via Bar menu -> System Settings.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
Three status glyphs sit left of the Bar clock; each opens a control
panel on click:
.TP
.B Volume
Speaker glyph; panel shows the software volume level bar with
"-" / "+" buttons (click adjusts by 10, range 0-100; no audio
hardware yet).
.TP
.B Network
Signal-bar glyph reflecting the live \fIS_NETINFO\fR interface state:
three bars when up, dimmed with an X when down. The panel shows the
eth0 state and IP address, refreshed by the 1 Hz Bar repaint.
.TP
.B Bluetooth
Rune glyph; panel offers a Radio On/Off software toggle (icon follows
the state) and reports adapter detection. QEMU i386 has no class-0xD
wireless controller, so it honestly reports "Adapter: none".
.SH SETTINGS PERSISTENCE
The wallpaper theme, volume and bluetooth switch persist in
\fI/etc/desktop.cfg\fR (plain-text key=value). Every change writes
the file immediately; Sprach reloads it before its first paint, so
boot shows the last saved wallpaper.
.SH DESKTOP ICONS
An app icon grid sits on the work-area wallpaper (single surface,
reusing the Launchpad /bin scan and icon assets), always at the bottom
of the window z-order. Click an icon to launch the app; clicks reach
the desktop only after every panel, menu and window declined them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR copland (7),
.BR sprach (7)
